{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1544210925,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ0NTMzOTQ2Ng==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3074#issuecomment-445339466"},"message":"\u003e If I `run` a command with `--explicit` there seems to be no way to rerun it.\n\nMeaning you can't rerun it with a dirty repo, right?\n\nThat's by design in the sense that I didn't intend for `--explicit` to lift rerun's clean repo requirement (The primary motivation was to \"extend the run API to support all the running aspects without the result capture\", gh-2593.)  Given rerun's clean repo requirement, \"add only these outputs\" behavior loses most of its point since we know the repo started off clean and, if there are downstream commits in the rerun sequence, the sequence shouldn't proceed with a dirty repository.\n\nPerhaps we should teach rerun about `--explicit`, but why is not clear to me yet.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1544210925,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE2MDAxNDQ1NA=="},"target":"2d228ee293641c15bcbc48cfdc5fd11a9e6aee1c057941181633c9cac7548c99","message":"\u003e If I `run` a command with `--explicit` there seems to be no way to rerun it.\n\nMeaning you can't rerun it with a dirty repo, right?\n\nThat's by design in the sense that I didn't intend for `--explicit` to lift rerun's clean repo requirement (The primary motivation for `--explicit` was to \"extend the run API to support all the running aspects without the result capture\", gh-2593.)  Given rerun's clean repo requirement, \"add only these outputs\" behavior loses most of its point since we know the repo started off clean and, if there are downstream commits in the rerun sequence, the sequence shouldn't proceed with a dirty repository.\n\nPerhaps we should teach rerun about `--explicit`, but why is not clear to me yet.","files":null