s/3074#issuecomment-494938652"},"message":"\u003e FWIW, dirty or not, with current speed of `status` on rich hierarchies (#3311, and \"resolved\" #3342), `--explicit` is the only way to `run` anything without waiting for minutes for an initial feedback on either \"it is all kosher\".\n\nWorth noting, though from my POV that's an issue to deal with in `status` (or some alternative approach) rather than a reason to add --explicit to rerun.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1561727022,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjcyNjAwNw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3074#issuecomment-506726007"},"message":"I just keep running into it over and over again.  Some times it is \"speed\", some times it is just a matter of having some unrelated (to `rerun`) uncommitted changes still present.  I would really appreciate this to be supported... I will look into sending a PR later today/tomorrow","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1561729618,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjc0MDA4MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3074#issuecomment-506740080"},"message":"Given that nobody else has weighed in and you're footing the bill, as you wish.  I'll move this to the top of the queue and submit a PR.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1561748398,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUwNjg0MzY0NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3074#issuecomment-506843645"},"message":"Thank you!","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1562592803,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjQ2NjE2MjQyNg=="},"status":2}]}